        "body": "Dear author, I noticed that in the paper it mentioned \"we choose the improved COCO Caption dataset proposed by ShareGPT4V\", and the readme.md says \"for coco , the data need to be a JSON or JSONL file, you can refer to [sharegpt4v](https://github.com/InternLM/InternLM-XComposer/blob/main/projects/ShareGPT4V/docs/Data.md#prepare-images) for data preparation.\" as well . However, the original ShareGPT4V Dataset contains a lot of different dataset in a single json, so should I produce the dataset myself by using the GPT4V? I'm quite infamiliar with this dataset, so being very confused. Many thanks.  ",
